  "question": {
    "text": "When a hydrocarbon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> undergoes combustion in the presence of air, it requires <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math> equivalents of oxygen and produces <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> equivalents of water. What is the molecular formula of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>?",
